# Live Chapter 1 content, ported from existing scenes; Codex integration 2026-09-09.
NPC: steward
LOCATION: lounge

TOPIC: default
  GATE: steward_ready AND NOT topic_done(steward, steward_open)
  TAG: steward_open
  VOICE: trombone_bureaucratic_medium_v2
  THE CLUB'S STEWARD: "He sets down the glass he was drying.\n\nNot used to seeing you without the badge, Officer."
  WALTER CORWIN: "I'm not asking as the badge today."
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v1
  THE CLUB'S STEWARD: "Didn't figure you were.\n\nAsk, then. I'll keep drying these."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: day = 3 AND coat != plain
  TAG: steward_badge
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_short_v1
  THE STEWARD: "I asked you to leave your badge behind."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: day < 3 AND evidence(service_work)
  TAG: steward_first_lead
  TIME: 4
  WALTER CORWIN: "Mrs. Almy says a woman came around asking about work here. Cleaning, laundry, anything she could carry home."
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v2
  THE STEWARD: "I heard the same, secondhand. Never caught a name.\n\nColored woman, I was told. That's the whole of what reached me."
  WALTER CORWIN: "Who would have taken her name down, if anyone did?"
  VOICE: trombone_bureaucratic_long_v1
  THE STEWARD: "If a name was taken, it would be in the staff day book. The dining-room list is no use to you.\n\nNot now, Officer. I have the room to put in order."
  NOTEBOOK: steward_first_lead_1 | "The steward heard secondhand that a colored woman had asked about work at the estate; he never caught a name and won't say who told him."
  EVIDENCE: steward_heard_secondhand

TOPIC: default
  GATE: day < 3
  TAG: steward_first
  WALTER CORWIN: "I need to ask about the people who came through the service entrance."
  VOICE: trombone_haunting_medium_v2
  THE STEWARD: "Then ask for the day book. The seating list is for the dining room. It won't tell you who came to work."
  WALTER CORWIN: "May I see the day book?"
  VOICE: trombone_bureaucratic_medium_v2
  THE STEWARD: "Not while I'm putting this room in order, Officer. Come back another day."
  NOTEBOOK: first_day_book | "The steward distinguishes the staff day book from the dining-room seating list. He has not produced it. Ask for the day book on returning."

TOPIC: day_book
  GATE: steward_ready AND evidence(service_work) AND NOT topic_done(steward, day_book)
  TAG: steward_day_book
  LABEL: "Ask for the staff day book he mentioned"
  TIME: 4
  WALTER CORWIN: "You said the staff had a separate book. Mrs. Almy remembers Naomi asking for work here."
  [The steward takes a narrow ruled book from beneath the sideboard.]
  THE DAY BOOK: "N. FREEMAN — DAY WORK — KITCHEN WING."
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v1
  THE STEWARD: "That is the entry. Copy it as it stands. I did not write her full name."
  WALTER CORWIN: "Who can identify her?"
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v1
  THE STEWARD: "The woman at the boardinghouse knew her. You have already spoken to her."
  WALTER CORWIN: "And the seventh place setting? You always laid seven chairs for six men."
  [The steward wipes the rim of an empty wine goblet with slow, circular strokes.]
  VOICE: trombone_haunting_long_v2
  THE STEWARD: "Standing instruction from Judge Wexford. Fork to the right, knife edge turned outward.\nOld whaler's custom for a man lost at sea whose body never came home."
  WALTER CORWIN: "They were setting a plate for a drowned man?"
  VOICE: trombone_bureaucratic_medium_v2
  THE STEWARD: "They were setting a plate for whoever was willing to sit in the chair, Officer.\nToward the end, nobody asked who it was."
  NOTEBOOK: day_book_entry | "Staff day book records 'N. Freeman — Day Work — Kitchen Wing.' Steward revealed the seventh place setting was laid with inverted cutlery—an old whaler's table setting for unrecovered drowned dead."
  EVIDENCE: estate_day_book

TOPIC: club_talk
  GATE: steward_ready
  TAG: club_talk
  LABEL: "Ask what the members used to talk about"
  TIME: 4
  THE SMOKING LOUNGE: "The steward sets a glass on the sideboard. Walter asks about the conversations he used to overhear while serving the members."
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v1
  THE STEWARD: "They stopped speaking of power, toward the end.\n\nStarted speaking, tenderly, of her."
  NOTEBOOK: "Toward the end of what, he doesn't say.\nHer, he doesn't explain.\n\nWalter writes both down exactly as given."
  EVIDENCE: club_talk

TOPIC: club_devotion
  GATE: steward_ready AND evidence(club_talk)
  TAG: club_devotion
  LABEL: "Ask what Kessler used to say"
  TIME: 4
  VOICE: trombone_haunting_medium_v2
  THE STEWARD: "Kessler said it more than once. She'll have us home.\n\nSaid she's no different from any mother."
  NOTEBOOK: "A butcher, a judge, a doctor, a district attorney, a man of property, all of them speaking the same sentence about the same absent woman.\n\nNone of them ever named her."
  EVIDENCE: club_devotion

TOPIC: pantry_lead
  GATE: steward_ready AND evidence(club_devotion)
  TAG: pantry_lead
  LABEL: "Ask about the old pantry door"
  TIME: 5
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_long_v1
  THE STEWARD: "There's gin left from before the war. Behind the old pantry door.\n\nThey boarded it up during a renovation and never finished unboarding it. Nobody goes back there. Nobody's gone back there in years."
  WALTER CORWIN: "Will you show me?"
  VOICE: trombone_dismissive_short_v2
  THE STEWARD: "No."
  NOTEBOOK: "He won't say why. He also won't take back the direction he just gave.\n\nThe kitchen wing. The old pantry."
  EVIDENCE: pantry_lead

